<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Clann Ruaidhrí</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as MacRuairi kindred</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Clann Ruaidhrí was a medieval kindred of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrides">Hebrides</a> and western Highlands descended from Ruaidhrí, grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somerled">Somerled</a>. Its leaders held Garmoran, Uist and other lands and were among the leading sea-lords of the Isles in the 13th and 14th centuries. The male line ended with the murder of Ranald MacRuairi in 1346, after which the marriage of his sister Amy to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-of-islay">John of Islay</a> brought its lands to the MacDonald Lords of the Isles.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/clann-ruaidhri.jpg" alt="Clann Ruaidhrí" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mike Searle · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Castle_Tioram_-_geograph.org.uk_-_966396.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
